  "notes": [
    "Kill-without-signal initially survived because the 150ms deadline could expire before the executable reached its first statement. Final termination grading uses cancellation after a real readiness marker, with inherited-descendant end-state inspection. Short deadline is tested separately.",
    "Two strengthened deadline baselines failed their added PID-readiness assertion (Node and shell fixtures) because the process had not reached user code before 150ms. They are invalid fixture assumptions, not production failures. Final assertion verifies ETIMEDOUT and settlement; actual launched-process termination is proven independently.",
    "Layout cleanup initially survived because an empty layout conversion routes to fallback before merge. Final layout fixture retains page 2 and omits scanned page 1, asserts the text-layer merge was reached, and tests actual job removal. All exploratory survivor receipts are excluded from final kills.",
    "A restored baseline failed a one-second readiness wait on a fresh executable; fixture-readiness-baseline.log retains the failure. Final readiness waits allow up to three seconds, and inherited-worker cancellation first observes the descendant running. No existing suite timeout or assertion changed."
